#! ia 1.0

@schema task
  lowers to definition
  sections
    must have meaning
    must have work
    may have relationships
    closed
  fields
    must have meaning.says as text
    may have meaning.answers as text
    must have work.title as text
    must have work.status as id in [proposed, open, held, closed, dropped, superseded]
    must have work.milestone as ref to milestone
    may have work.owner as text
    may have work.start as text form iso-date
    may have work.due as text form iso-date
    may have work.ended as text form iso-date
    may have work.source as text
    may have work.action as text "What the task's owner does to complete it."
    may have work.expected-artifact as text "The artifact the task produces, as a path or name."
    may have work.exit-evidence as ref to observation "The observation whose success verdict closes the task."
    may have work.owner-agent as ref to agent "The agent that owns the task; work.owner stays the free-text owner."
  edges
    may require task one-or-more
    may require milestone one-or-more
    may require decision one-or-more
    may supersede task one
